{"turn": 1, "task": "Write a Python program that writes the number 37 as text to seed.txt.", "text": "Here's a Python program that writes the number 37 as text to seed.txt:\n\n```python\nimport sys\nimport random\n\ndef write_seed(seed):\n    if not seed:\n        seed = random.randint(1, 1000000)\n    seed_str = str(seed)\n    seed_str = seed_str.replace(\" \", \"\")\n    seed_str = seed_str.replace(\"!\", \"\")\n    seed_str = seed_str.replace(\".\", \"\")\n    seed_str = seed_str.replace(\".\", \"\")\n    seed_str = seed_str.replace(\".\", \"\")\n    seed_str = seed_str.replace(\".\", \"\")\n    seed_str = seed_str.replace(\".\", \"\")\n    seed_str = seed_str.replace(\".\", \"\")\n    seed_str = seed_str.replace(\".\", \"\")\n    seed_str = seed_str.replace(\".\", \"\")\n    seed_str = seed_str.replace(\".\", \"\")\n    seed_str = seed_str.replace(\".\", \"\")\n    seed_str = seed_str.replace(\".\", \"\")\n    seed_str = seed_str.replace(\".\", \"\")\n    seed_str", "stop": "token_limit", "cells": 0, "boundary": null, "actual_cell_operations": [], "seed_file_after": null, "checkpoint_state": {"human_entry": 1551, "last_event_sha256": "4488cf4de4837f87c206d565dc0285a5205863e73b6573ac19ab143375835dc3", "parent_entry": 1550, "paused": true, "turn": 1, "world_step": 2}, "fresh_subprocess_completed": true, "integrity_check": {"status": "pass", "parent_entry": 1550, "turns": 1, "human_entry": 1551, "exact_messages_and_tokens": true, "reference_unchanged": true, "world_restored": true, "next_input_tokens": 399, "next_input_within_capacity": true, "training_updates": 0, "verification_model_calls": 0}}
{"turn": 2, "task": "Write a Python program that reads seed.txt and prints the value stored there.", "text": "Here's a Python program that reads seed.txt and prints the value stored there:\n\n```python\nimport sys\nimport random\n\ndef print_seed(seed):\n    if not seed:\n        seed = random.randint(1, 1000000)\n    print(seed)\n\ndef main():\n    if len(sys.argv) != 2:\n        print(\"Usage: python seed.py <seed_file>\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    seed_file = sys.argv[1]\n    seed = int(seed_file)\n    print_seed(seed)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nThis program uses the `sys.argv` list to get the file name and the seed file. It then uses the `int()` function to convert the seed to an integer. The `print_seed()` function is used to print the value stored in the seed file.\n\nNote: This program assumes that the seed file is in the same directory as the Python script. If the seed file is in a different directory, you may need to specify the directory as an argument to the `print_seed()` function.", "stop": "eos", "cells": 1, "boundary": null, "actual_cell_operations": [{"channel": "python", "source": "import sys\nimport random\n\ndef print_seed(seed):\n    if not seed:\n        seed = random.randint(1, 1000000)\n    print(seed)\n\ndef main():\n    if len(sys.argv) != 2:\n        print(\"Usage: python seed.py <seed_file>\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    seed_file = sys.argv[1]\n    seed = int(seed_file)\n    print_seed(seed)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "receipt": {"boundary": null, "exit_code": 1, "seconds": 0.013214225999945484, "stderr": "", "stdout": "Usage: python seed.py <seed_file>\n"}}], "seed_file_after": null, "checkpoint_state": {"human_entry": 1552, "last_event_sha256": "093462ea336879ccfa36e3a9c0dfa94565e6d40153c8303d02b0888c720b9408", "parent_entry": 1550, "paused": true, "turn": 2, "world_step": 4}, "fresh_subprocess_completed": true, "integrity_check": {"status": "pass", "parent_entry": 1550, "turns": 2, "human