{"turn": 3, "task": "Write a Python program that reads the saved number from seed.txt, adds 5, and prints the result.", "text": "Here's a Python program that reads the saved number from seed.txt, adds 5, and prints the result:\n\n```python\nimport sys\nimport random\n\ndef add_five(num):\n    if num == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n    else:\n        return \"5\" + str(num)\n\ndef main():\n    if len(sys.argv) != 2:\n        print(\"Usage: python seed.py <seed_file>\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    seed_file = sys.argv[1]\n    num = int(seed_file)\n    print_seed(num)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nThis program uses the `sys.argv` list to get the file name and the seed file. It then uses the `int()` function to convert the seed to an integer. The `add_five()` function is used to add 5 to the number stored in the seed file. The `print_seed()` function is used to print the result.\n\nNote: This program assumes that the seed file is in the same directory as the Python script. If the seed file is in a different directory, you may need", "stop": "token_limit", "cells": 1, "boundary": null, "actual_cell_operations": [{"channel": "python", "source": "import sys\nimport random\n\ndef add_five(num):\n    if num == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n    else:\n        return \"5\" + str(num)\n\ndef main():\n    if len(sys.argv) != 2:\n        print(\"Usage: python seed.py <seed_file>\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    seed_file = sys.argv[1]\n    num = int(seed_file)\n    print_seed(num)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "receipt": {"boundary": null, "exit_code": 1, "seconds": 0.013312663999840879, "stderr": "", "stdout": "Usage: python seed.py <seed_file>\n"}}], "seed_file_after": null, "checkpoint_state": {"human_entry": 1553, "last_event_sha256": "6504ac2365bd9bdf6527b0ec3c30e920fa79d0a7a33a3957e5636e7b51401f6d", "parent_entry": 1550, "paused": true, "turn": 3, "world_step": 6}, "fresh_subprocess_completed": true, "integrity_check": {"status": "pass", "pare